posts.body:
@funkyvibes
.gainMP() won't work, the correct version of that is .gainMp()
Also, you shouldn't need to do the whole $gameActors thing. That notetag should allow you to use target instead and it will target the actor that is affected by the state.
So try:  target.gainMp(20);
Edit: So, I double checked and to make the state look for equipment, you'd use this script:
target.hasWeapon($dataWeapons[ID])
target.hasArmor($dataArmors[ID])
depending on if you're searching for armor or weapon, and then you change the ID to the database ID of the specific equipment you're checking for. You want to create a conditional on the Passive state based on that, and that would look something like this:
JavaScript:
<Custom Passive Condition>
  if (target.hasWeapon($dataWeapons[ID])) {
    condition = true;
  } else {
    condition = false;
  }
  </Custom Passive Condition>

<Custom Turn Start Effect>

target.gainMp(20);

 </Custom Turn Start Effect>
